lane: backlog-audit
why: the channel entries have gone stale. channel-sentinel-default is
  filed as open and Channel.apply already dispatches on capacity --
  I landed it and did not clear the entry. A stale backlog is worse
  than a short one: the next agent takes a lane, runs a gate, and
  finds the work already done.
how: audit every channel/chunk/feed entry against the code, close what
  is done (with the commit that did it), keep what is genuinely open,
  and correct anything whose premise a later measurement refuted.
  Also: sendManyNow has no production caller -- decide whether it gets
  one or goes, rather than leaving a public operation nobody uses.
